{{en-noun}}

# A [[ward]] in a detached building connected with a [[hospital]].

{{etymon|en|id=line or portion|:inh|enm:trayne<t:train><ety:der<fro:train<id:delay><ety:der<fro:trainer<alt:traïner><id:drag>>>>>|tree=1}}
From {{inh|en|enm|trayne|t=train}}, from {{der|en|fro|train|t=a delay, a drawing out}}, from {{m|fro|traïner|t=to pull out, to draw}}, from {{der|en|la-vul|*traginō}}, from {{m|la|*tragō}}, from {{der|en|la|trahō|t=to pull, to draw}}, ultimately from {{der|en|ine-pro|*dʰregʰ-|*tregʰ-|to pull, draw, drag}}. The verb was derived from the noun in Middle English.

For the meaning ''to teach'' compare typologically {{m+|ru|ната́скивать}} (akin to {{m|ru|тащи́ть}}).

{{etymon|en|id=gerund noun|:inh|enm:-ynge<id:gerund noun>}}
{{inh+|en|enm|-ing}}, {{m|enm|-yng}}, {{m|enm|-ynge}}, from {{inh|en|ang|-ing}}, {{m|ang|-ung|t=-ing|pos=suffix forming nouns from verbs}}, from {{inh|en|gmw-pro|*-ingu}}, {{m|gmw-pro|*-ungu}}, from {{inh|en|gem-pro|*-ungō|*-ingō, *-ungō|t=-ing}}. 
